ut even with morality  rishta side chances are that none of us  would know jay-z's name if he hadn't  chosen the life of rhyme above the life  of  I he wouldn't be worth a billion dollars  he probably wouldn't have won Beyonce's  heart and the odds are high that he'd be  incarcerated if not dead here's how  jay-z described to success years later  the reach that this music had for me was  unbelievable of course luck plays a part  in it but every human being has genius  level talent there are no chosen ones  you have to find what you're great at  and tap into it pursuing a career in  music wasn't just about making a better  ethical and lifestyle choice it was also  about making the right career choice the  choice to do something he loved  something he could get paid well for and  something he was skilled at you might  not be facing the same dilemma between  drug dealing and superstardom but you  can use a similar method of analysis to  make your own career choices
 

